From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: the chunk step carries its start and prompt length again

0007 rewrote the prompt chunk protocol: the step now carries its rows in the
header's flags (bits 16 and up) instead of deriving them, and the follower reads
start and length from the header's depth and top_k (cuda_follow's chunk handler:
prefillChunk(ids, h.depth, chunkRows(h), h.top_k, ...)). The ported leader never
set those two fields, so every follower received depth=0 and top_k=0 and raised
PromptTooLong on the first prompt of any chat request (len == 0):

  error: rank 1: following rank 0 stopped (PromptTooLong)

The source era sets both on the send (.depth = start, .top_k = ids.len); this
restores them, which is what the follower has always read.

Gates: the chat completes on TP=3 (the smoke's count 1..20) with every rank's
digests equal across arms; recorded in PORT-LEDGER.
diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_follow.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_follow.zig
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_follow.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_follow.zig
@@ -247,7 +247,7 @@
         const n = (if (wide) engine.chunkEnd(a_end, ids.len, at) else a_end) - start; // this step's rows
         const part = ids[start..@min(ids.len, start + n + 1)];
         const split = sparse.splitAt(start, x.e.settings.index_split, x.e.share.world); // a paired step's chunks share it
-        try x.send(.{ .kind = @backingInt(Kind.chunk), .flags = x.rows() | @as(u32, @intFromBool(split)) << 1 | @as(u32, @intCast(n)) << 16, .a = if (from) |r| r.id else 0, .seed = if (from) |r| r.at else 0 }, part);
+        try x.send(.{ .kind = @backingInt(Kind.chunk), .flags = x.rows() | @as(u32, @intFromBool(split)) << 1 | @as(u32, @intCast(n)) << 16, .a = if (from) |r| r.id else 0, .seed = if (from) |r| r.at else 0, .depth = @intCast(start), .top_k = @intCast(ids.len) }, part);
         x.e.index_split = split;
         const first = try x.e.prefillChunk(part, start, n, ids.len, from, cancel, marks);
         return .{ .first = first, .rows = n };
